# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Wassell CRM — .gitignore
# Keeps secrets, build output, and heavy assets out of the repo.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/

# Environment variables — NEVER commit these
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
*.local

# The passphrase for the encrypted secrets bundle. Covered by *.local above;
# listed explicitly because committing it would defeat the entire scheme.
.secrets-passphrase.local

# Backups written by scripts/secrets/unseal.sh when it would overwrite a
# locally-modified secret file.
*.bak

# NOT ignored, deliberately: secrets/wassel-secrets.enc is AES-256 ciphertext
# and is meant to be committed — that is how cloud sessions get their secrets.
# See docs/cloud-session-setup.md.

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
logs/
# Exception: the activity-log source directory (case-insensitive matches `logs/`
# on Windows / macOS and was being ignored).
!src/pages/Logs/
*.log

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Claude / local scratch
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/plans/
.claude/hooks/*.log

# Python bytecode from the deck/research skills under .claude/skills
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Brand assets are COMMITTED (11 MB of logos/palette PNGs). The deck skills
# need them, and a cloud session has no other way to get them. They are public
# marketing material, so a public repo is fine. Kept out of the production
# bundle by not being imported from src/ — not by being gitignored.

# Unrelated side project that happens to live in this folder — NOT part of Wassell.
# It's a separate Supabase Edge Function (haberchat-webhook / WhatsApp bot). Keep
# it out of the Wassell repo so the two projects don't get tangled. Everything
# else under supabase/functions/ (the marketing pipeline agents + the inbox +
# _shared helpers) IS part of Wassell and lives in git.
supabase/functions/haberchat-webhook/
# Deno lock/cache noise inside function dirs
supabase/functions/**/deno.lock
supabase/functions/**/.deno/

# TypeScript build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# OS junk
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.vercel
.env*.local
tmp/
dbq.tmp.mjs

# Cached raw Overpass responses for the geo-intelligence builds — regenerable
# via `node data/source/geo/fetch.mjs` (12 MB+, and re-fetching is the point of
# having the cache locally, not of shipping it).
data/source/geo/raw/
data/source/geo-uae/raw/

# Cached OSM admin-boundary relations (country/region) — regenerable via
# `node data/source/geo/fetch-admin.mjs`.
data/source/geo/raw-admin/

# Geo build outputs that are pure derivatives of
# data/source/geo/saudi-cities-geo-intelligence.json (which IS committed — it is
# what the importer consumes). Regenerate with `node data/source/geo/process.mjs`.
data/source/geo/saudi-cities-geo-intelligence.geojson
data/source/geo/saudi-cities-geo-intelligence.csv
# 9.6 MB intermediate: the OSM admin relations are already imported into
# geo_admin_boundaries, and `node data/source/geo/fetch-admin.mjs` rebuilds it.
data/source/geo/admin-boundaries.json
docs/marketing-reference/tools/node_modules/
docs/marketing-reference/tools/render-page.html
.mos-branch.local
.mos-branch.env

# Local-only dev API shim + vite override (Windows `vercel dev` workaround) — not
# part of the app; each developer keeps their own. See CLAUDE.md dev notes.
dev-api-shim.mjs
vite.config.local.mjs
.kimi-logs/
